body:
1. Steps to reproduce the problem:
   1. Create a model.. any model (extending \Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model)
   2. Create a simple trait to add a GlobalScope for the model
   3. Create a simple ScopeInterface implementation
   4. use a `$builder->where( ... )` (or any derivative like orWhere) with a closure as argument in it's `apply($builder)` method.
2. Expected outcome: The sql it's generated and executed normally
3. Received outcome: The sql generation loops forever until filling server memory, if launch with `php artisan serve` it simply throws a Segmentation Fault on the console.

Configuration:

```
$ php -v
PHP 5.5.17-2+deb.sury.org~precise+1 (cli) (built: Sep 25 2014 09:07:54) 
Copyright (c) 1997-2014 The PHP Group
Zend Engine v2.5.0, Copyright (c) 1998-2014 Zend Technologies
    with Zend OPcache v7.0.4-dev, Copyright (c) 1999-2014, by Zend Technologies
```

laravel 4.2: Using the workbench to create a package (no namespaces issues).

Code:

Simple model: Stock.php

```
<?php namespace Company\Package;

use \Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model as Eloquent;

class Stock extends Eloquent {

    use LocalizedTrait;

}
```

Simple trait: LocalizedTrait.php

```
<?php namespace Company\Package;

trait LocalizedTrait {

    public static function bootLocalizedTrait()
    {
        static::addGlobalScope(new LocalizedScope);
    }

}
```

Simple ScopeInterface implementation: LocalizedScope.php

```
<?php namespace Company\Package;

use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Builder;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\ScopeInterface;

class LocalizedScope extends ScopeInterface {

    public function apply(Builder $builder)
    {

            $builder->where("language_id", '=', 1); // This works

            $builder->orWhere(function($query) { $query->where("language_id", '=', 2); }); // This doesn't

    }

// .. the class goes on.. with the implementation of the ScopeInterface...
```
